{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-hyperelliptic-z5-classification","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:hyperelliptic-z5-classification","kind":"theorem","title":"Minimal-genus hyperelliptic curves with faithful $\\mathbb{Z}_5$-symmetry","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hyperelliptic-quintic"],"cites":["references/bolza1887"],"tags":["riemann-hurwitz","hyperelliptic","z5","classification","minimal-genus"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.minimal_z5_classification","text":"hyperelliptic-z5-classification.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hyperelliptic-z5-classification.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:hyperelliptic-z5-classification\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> be a smooth projective Riemann surface of minimal genus satisfying two conditions:</em></p>\n<p><em>(i) <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> is hyperelliptic. There exists a degree-2 morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi \\colon X \\to \\mathbb{P}^1</code> with involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\iota</code>.</em>\n<em>(ii) <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> admits a faithful <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_5</code> automorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\phi</code> commuting with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\iota</code>.</em></p>\n<p><em>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g(X) = 2</code>. The surface <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> is isomorphic to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{X}_5 \\colon y^2 = x^5 - 1</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hyperelliptic-z5-classification.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"11.13.1"}
